# Last known RunPod connection details.
#
#   set -a; . runpod/pod.env; set +a
#   ssh root@$POD_IP -p $POD_PORT -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#   scp -P $POD_PORT somefile root@$POD_IP:/workspace/minimax/refs/
#
# ⚠️ THESE GO STALE. RunPod assigns a new IP and port on every pod creation, so
# treat this as a starting guess, not truth. If ssh says "Connection refused" or
# the proxy says "container not found", the pod was replaced - get fresh details
# from the console (Connect -> "SSH over exposed TCP") or the RunPod MCP server,
# then UPDATE AND COMMIT THIS FILE so the next agent isn't stuck too.
#
# The IP is ephemeral infrastructure in a private repo, not a secret.
# The private key is NOT here and must never be committed.

